diff --git a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
index 6bddff1..4b84036 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
@@ -96,3 +96,31 @@ __Request:__
 __Response:__
 
 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
+## `POST /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions`
+
+Registers a browser's web push subscription for the current user, so whatever lands in their notifications tray also reaches that device. Pass along the subscription the browser got from its push service. Registering the same subscription again is a no-op.
+
+Only the current user can register their own subscriptions; other users get `403 Forbidden`.
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `endpoint` | string | Yes | The push service URL of the subscription |
+| `p256dh_key` | string | Yes | The subscription's `p256dh` key, base64url-encoded |
+| `auth_key` | string | Yes | The subscription's `auth` secret, base64url-encoded |
+
+__Request:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "push_subscription": {
+    "endpoint": "https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send/abc123",
+    "p256dh_key": "BNcRd...",
+    "auth_key": "tBHI..."
+  }
+}
+```
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` on success.
diff --git a/docs/development.md b/docs/development.md
index b8c3e65..5791372 100644
--- a/docs/development.md
+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -56,6 +56,14 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Push notifications
+
+Web push notifications are signed with a VAPID key pair. In development and test, a pair is generated on first boot and kept in `tmp/vapid_key.json`, so you can turn notifications on for your browser from the notification settings right away. To use a specific pair instead, set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` in the environment. You can generate one with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails web_push:vapid_key
+```
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
